<title>SPAIN: ATHLETICS-SALAMANCA INTERNATIONAL RESULTS.</title>
<headline>ATHLETICS-SALAMANCA INTERNATIONAL RESULTS.</headline>
<dateline>SALAMANCA, Spain 1997-07-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Selected winners of an international meeting on Monday:</p>
<p>Men</p>
<p>100 metres: Linford Christie (Britain) 10.12 seconds</p>
<p>400 metres: Davis Kamoga (Uganda) 45.11</p>
<p>400 metres hurdles: Sammy Matete (Zambia) 49.08</p>
<p>1,500 metres: Venuste Niyangabo (Burundi) 3 minutes 34.70</p>
<p>seconds</p>
<p>High jump: Javier Sotomayor (Cuba) 2.34 metres</p>
<p>Long jump: Eric Walder (U.S.)  8.27</p>
<p>Triple jump: Rogel Nachum (Israel) 16.84</p>
<p>Women 400 metres: Idalmis Bonne (Cuba) 51.83</p>
<p>400 metres hurdles: Daimi Pernia (Cuba) 55.89</p>
<p>Triple jump: Olga Cepero (Cuba) 14.16</p>
<p>Men</p>
<p>800 metres: Norbert Tellez (Cuba) 1:46.74</p>
<p>110 metres hurdles: Igor Kovacs (Slovakia) 13.18 (wind</p>
<p>assisted)</p>
<p>Women</p>
<p>800 metres: Ana Menendez (Spain) 2:04.63</p>
<p>100 metres hurdles: Ludmila Engquist (Sweden) 12.54 (wind</p>
<p>assisted)</p>
<p>Discus: Angeles Barreiro (Spain) 49.72</p>
